            <p>London Heathrow processed over 79 million passengers annually before pandemic disruptions, ranking as Europe's busiest airport and one of the world's most significant aviation nodes. Its five terminals and extensive long-haul network make it the natural destination for San Diego's transatlantic aspirations. </p>

            <h2>Airlines Flying from San Diego to London</h2>
            <p>The competitive landscape on this route is shaped by limited nonstop capacity and abundant connecting alternatives through major West Coast and Midwest hubs. </p>

            <h3>Full-Service Carriers</h3>
            <p><b>British Airways</b></p>
            <p>British Airways operates the sole nonstop service on this route, a testament to San Diego's economic importance and leisure appeal. </p>

            <p><b>Signature elements:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Nonstop service from SAN to London Heathrow, typically operating daily during peak season and reduced frequency in winter</li>
                <li>Boeing 777-200ER and Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner deployment</li>
                <li>Evening departures (around 7:30 PM) arriving in London early afternoon the following day</li>
                <li>Executive Club Avios earning with extensive partner redemption possibilities</li>
                <li>Club World business class featuring lie-flat seats and British dining</li>
                <li>Strong connections throughout the UK, Europe, Africa, and Asia beyond London</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>American Airlines</h3>
            <p>American competes through its oneworld partnership with British Airways and its Dallas and Phoenix hubs. </p>

            <p><b>Key characteristics:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>No current nonstop service from San Diego to London</li>
                <li>Connections through Dallas-Fort Worth (DFW) and Phoenix (PHX) with well-timed onward segments</li>
                <li>AAdvantage program earning with reciprocal benefits on British Airways</li>
                <li>Flagship Business class on transatlantic segments</li>
                <li>Strong San Diego market presence through regional operations</li>
            </ul>
