            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>Q1: Are there direct flights from San Diego to London?</h3>
            <p>British Airways operates nonstop service from San Diego to London Heathrow, typically daily during peak season and reduced frequency in winter. This is currently the only nonstop option on this route. </p>


            <h3>Q2: What is the cheapest time to fly from San Diego to London?</h3>
            <p>January and February offer the lowest fares, with economy round-trips often available at $550-$900. Summer months command premium pricing. Book 45-60 days ahead for best peak-season rates. </p>


            <h3>Q3: Do US citizens need a visa for the UK?</h3>
            <p>No visa required for tourism or business stays under six months. A valid passport with six months remaining validity suffices—no additional documentation needed for standard visits. </p>


            <h3>Q4: Should I fly from San Diego or drive to LAX for London flights?</h3>
            <p>British Airways nonstop from San Diego offers ultimate convenience. However, LAX provides vastly more options, often at lower prices. The 120-mile drive (2-3 hours) may be worthwhile for significant savings or preferred schedules. </p>


            <h3>Q5: How do I get from Heathrow airport to central London?</h3>
            <p>Heathrow Express reaches Paddington in 15 minutes for approximately £25. The Elizabeth Line connects to central London in 35-40 minutes for £12-£15. The Tube takes 45-60 minutes for approximately £6. Taxis cost £50-£80. </p>


            <h3>Q6: Can I use US dollars in London?</h3>
            <p>The pound sterling (£) is the UK's currency. US dollars are not accepted. Credit cards work universally; contactless payment preferred. ATMs plentiful throughout the city. Notify your bank before travel. </p>


            <h3>Q7: What should I pack for London from San Diego?</h3>
            <p>Comfortable walking shoes essential for cobblestones and museum marathons. Layers for unpredictable weather. Waterproof jacket. Smart casual attire for theater and dining—universal power adapter for UK outlets (Type G). Remember London is significantly cooler than San Diego year-round. </p>


            <h3>Q8: Is London safe for American tourists?</h3>
            <p>London is generally safe with standard urban precautions. Pickpockets operate in tourist zones and on the Tube. Violent crime against tourists is rare. Police presence visible. Emergency number is 999. </p>


            <h3>Q9: What is the best way to avoid jet lag flying San Diego to London?</h3>
            <p>The eight-hour time difference requires significant adjustment. Choose evening departures arriving in London in the afternoon. Sleep on the flight. Upon arrival, expose yourself to daylight immediately, stay active until local evening, and avoid napping. Hydration throughout the journey is essential. </p>


            <h3>Q10: Can I visit other European cities easily from London?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Eurostar trains connect London to Paris (2h 15m), Brussels (2h), and Amsterdam (3h 40m). Budget airlines serve European destinations from London airports. Ferries connect to France and the Netherlands. Consider open-jaw tickets for multi-city itineraries. </p>


